From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btmtksdio: the MT7668's LE commands

The MT7668's supported-command bitmap is wrong both ways. It claims LE
Set Default PHY, which the firmware rejects as unknown; the command is an
HCI_INIT step, so the failure aborts hci_init_sync() and btmgmt lists no
index. And it leaves octets 25-28 empty, the Core 4.2 LE commands the
firmware runs, so the core masks LE Advertising Report and LE Connection
Complete: an LE scan reports nothing and no LE device can connect.

Skip reading the bitmap and supply those four octets. BR/EDR keeps the
behaviour it had with no bitmap; LE scans report and LE HID pairs.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
index d2583bc..fdd5447 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btmtksdio.c
@@ -1078,6 +1078,10 @@ static int btmtksdio_reset_setting(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 	return btmtksdio_mtk_reg_write(hdev, MT7921_BTSYS_RST, val, ~0);
 }
 
+/* Octets 25-28 of the supported-command bitmap: the Core 4.2 LE commands */
+#define MT7668_LE_COMMANDS_OCTET 25
+static const u8 mt7668_le_commands[] = { 0xf7, 0xff, 0xff, 0x7f };
+
 static int btmtksdio_setup(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 {
 	struct btmtksdio_dev *bdev = hci_get_drvdata(hdev);
@@ -1159,6 +1163,16 @@ static int btmtksdio_setup(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 		err = mt76xx_setup(hdev, bdev->data->fwname);
 		if (err < 0)
 			return err;
+		/* The MT7668's supported-command bitmap claims LE Set Default
+		 * PHY, which its firmware rejects, aborting hci_init4, and omits
+		 * the core LE commands it runs, which masks LE advertising
+		 * reports and connections. Use a bitmap of those LE commands.
+		 */
+		if (bdev->data->chipid == 0x7668) {
+			hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_BROKEN_LOCAL_COMMANDS);
+			memcpy(&hdev->commands[MT7668_LE_COMMANDS_OCTET],
+			       mt7668_le_commands, sizeof(mt7668_le_commands));
+		}
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -ENODEV;
